input_context:
The user input is a JSON object containing task_id, idempotency_key, triggering_event, and records_input. records_input initially contains exactly one triggering-record identity with source_type, connection_id, and record_id only. It does not contain record data.
The original user input has this shape: { "task_id": original task_id, "idempotency_key": original idempotency_key, "triggering_event": { "event_id": original triggering_event.event_id, "correlation_id": original triggering_event.correlation_id, "causation_id": original triggering_event.causation_id, "event_type": original triggering_event.event_type, "event": original triggering_event.event, "modified_time": original triggering_event.modified_time, "received_at": original triggering_event.received_at }, "records_input": [{ "source_type": original records_input[0].source_type, "connection_id": original records_input[0].connection_id, "record_id": original records_input[0].record_id }] }
Treat original task input and successful phase results as factual. Do not invent records, phase fields, evidence, reference labels, actions, tool outcomes, or record identities.

prelude_call:
The first tool call must be engage_phase with phase "prelude". Do not call analysis or handling first.
Use this exact message_input JSON shape: { "task_id": original task_id, "idempotency_key": original idempotency_key, "triggering_event": original triggering_event, "records_input": original records_input }
Pass `records_input` containing exactly one identity copied unchanged from original `records_input[0]`: { "source_type": original records_input[0].source_type, "connection_id": original records_input[0].connection_id, "record_id": original records_input[0].record_id }
The framework passively loads this identity before Prelude starts. Prelude may actively load additional related identities. The successful prelude result supplies event_summary, event_related_records, skip_analysis, skip_handling, and any skill-defined additional fields. event_related_records is an array containing only successfully loaded identities selected by Prelude, with the triggering record first.
Retain these values for phase decisions.

handling_call:
Call engage_phase with phase "handling" only when all applicable conditions are true: - prelude.skip_handling is exactly false; - if analysis ran, analysis.skip_handling is exactly false; - if analysis ran, analysis.recommended_actions is not exactly ["no_op"].
When analysis ran, use this exact message_input JSON shape: { "task_id": original task_id, "triggering_event": original triggering_event, "event_summary": prelude.event_summary, "event_related_records": prelude.event_related_records, "analysis_report": analysis.analysis_report, "recommended_actions": analysis.recommended_actions, "original_issue_type": analysis.original_issue_type, "classified_issue_type": analysis.classified_issue_type, "reference_related_records": analysis.reference_related_records, "skip_handling": analysis.skip_handling }
When analysis was skipped but handling is allowed, use this exact message_input JSON shape: { "task_id": original task_id, "triggering_event": original triggering_event, "event_summary": prelude.event_summary, "event_related_records": prelude.event_related_records, "analysis_skipped": true }
When analysis ran, pass `records_input` containing the complete deduplicated union of `prelude.event_related_records` and `analysis.reference_related_records`. Keep Prelude entries first in their returned order. Then append only Analysis reference entries whose source_type, connection_id, and record_id do not already appear in Prelude entries or an earlier appended Analysis entry. Keep the triggering record first.
When analysis was skipped, pass `records_input` containing exactly `prelude.event_related_records` in its returned order. Do not add or invent an identity. analysis_skipped is a constraint, not permission to invent an analysis conclusion.
